From cd9ae4110373176f17c515e39f34a3927fa90e5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:37:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(validator): say which party a finding is held
 against, and view a report for one
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A finding did not say who broke the clause. `mcp-conformance test` drives a
server with the official suite's client, and that client breaks clauses of its
own: it calls `logging/setLevel` on a server that never declared `logging`
(LIFE-009), and it opens a session and closes it without
`notifications/initialized` (LIFE-003). A server author read both as theirs.

Every requirement row now carries the registry's `actor`, and every finding a
`party`: the clause's actor when it binds one party, else — for a clause
binding both — the sender of the message at the finding's `seq`, else nobody.
The sender rule was checked against every `both` clause that has a check (the
15 at 2025-11-25 and the 24 at 2026-07-28): each points its finding at the
offending message itself, so the sender is the violator, and no check needed
a rule of its own. LIFE-003 points at the server's result and is held against
the client, because the registry types it `client`.

The party shows in every format: a leading `[client]`/`[server]` tag on the
human finding line, `party`/`actor` members in JSON (schema updated,
additive), `actor` and `party` properties on JUnit cases and in each
finding's location, `properties.party` on SARIF results and `properties.actor`
on rules, and pills in the HTML page.

`validate --party client|server` is an opt-in view: only that party's
findings, plus those held against nobody (labelled `[unattributed]`), count
toward the verdict and exit status; the verdict line reads `verdict (server
findings only): …` with what was set aside; JSON carries `party_view` and the
view's verdict; JUnit and SARIF set the other party's findings aside without
counting them; the default verdict and exit codes are unchanged.

